WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.020
The world’s fastest hunter

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.920
the peregrine falcon

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:12.640
snatches prey out of the sky at speeds of &gt;300 km/hr.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.760
This breakneck speed gives

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.060
these predators the element of surprise.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.060
It also lets them outmaneuver their prey,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.560
As you can see from this drone footage,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.280
it’s hard to study falcon attack dives

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.860
or “stoops” in real time.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.800
Because they happen so fast.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.620
So researchers turned to 3D simulations

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.880
of a computer-generated peregrine falcon

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.480
trying to catch a computer-generated starling.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.900
The team found that the falcon was best off diving

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.080
at roughly 150 km/hr.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.300
when the starling flew in a straight path.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.780
But if the starling was flying erratically

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.080
the falcon stood the greatest chance of success

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.440
by stooping at much higher speeds

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.290
around 360 km/hr.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.300
You’d think that the higher speeds would make it harder

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.780
for falcons to adjust to a moving target.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.420
But the opposite turned out to be true.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.609
Because they could generate more turning force

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.800
the predators were more maneuverable

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.130
at higher speeds.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:23.000
And it was only at these top speeds

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.640
that the falcons able to outmaneuver the agile starlings.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.800
So stoops don’t just help falcons overtake prey

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.820
they also help the predators change direction.

